      "open_issues": [
        "css-select 5.2.1 is a broken publish and cannot run on any input. subjects/css_select_latest/example.py keeps it in VERSIONS but excludes it from SYSTEMS via BROKEN, so the subject has five systems. Decide whether to keep that, or substitute (the rule as written has no clause for an uninstallable-in-effect release). css-select is deferred, so this does not affect tonight.",
        "jsonpath-plus 11.0.0 replaced the public JSONPath.cache object with module-level Maps and JSONPath.clearCache(). The domain runner's `JSONPath.cache = {}` reset is a no-op on 11.x, which would time evaluation only. subjects/jsonpath_plus_latest/node_runner.js calls clearCache() when it exists and falls back to the cache assignment for 10.x, so all six time parse + evaluate. subjects/jsonpath_js pins 10.4.0, so it is not affected today, but would be on upgrade."
      ]
